---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Moving from Nigeria to Canada: The Complete Guide | AfriMigrate"
  description="A complete, free guide to moving from Nigeria to Canada — Express Entry, Provincial Nominee Programs, costs, timelines and document tips."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/blog">Blog</a> / Nigeria to Canada</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">Guide · Nigeria → Canada</div>
  <h1>Moving from Nigeria to Canada: The Complete Guide</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    Nigerians consistently rank among the top source countries for Canadian permanent residence. Here's the realistic route, cost, and timeline — no consultant required.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step 1</div>
    <h2>Pick your pathway</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      Most Nigerian applicants without a Canadian job offer go through Express Entry, either on core CRS points alone or, more commonly, with a Provincial Nominee Program to add 600 points. Applicants with strong IELTS scores (CLB 9+) and a bachelor's degree assessed by an ECA body are usually well positioned.
    </p>
    <a href="/canada/express-entry" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Read the Express Entry guide →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step 2</div>
    <h2>Know your number</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      Calculate your CRS score before doing anything else — it tells you whether to aim for a general draw or focus your energy on a Provincial Nominee Program like Saskatchewan's SINP, which has historically been accessible to Nigerian applicants in healthcare, IT and skilled trades.
    </p>
    <a href="/canada/crs-calculator" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Calculate my CRS score →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step 3</div>
    <h2>Budget realistically</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      Between government fees, IELTS, ECA, police clearance and settlement funds, expect to need several thousand Canadian dollars in savings before you land — see our full breakdown for exact figures.
    </p>
    <a href="/canada/cost-of-moving" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">See the full cost breakdown →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step 4</div>
    <h2>Start your paperwork early</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      Nigerian police clearance certificates and document authentication can take longer than in other countries — start these the moment you decide to apply, not after you're invited.
    </p>
    <a href="/canada/document-checklist" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Build my document checklist →</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
